","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.01.20150123.full.mrc:424286006:1783","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_021.bib.mrc:89343649:3403"],"title":"Inviting death","dewey_decimal_class":["294.4/23"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Bibliography: p. 279-285.\nIncludes index."},"number_of_pages":324,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["88014503"],"subjects":["Suicide -- Religious aspects -- Jainism.","Spiritual life -- Jainism.","Jainism -- India -- Srāvana Belgola -- Customs and practices.","Sepulchral monuments -- India -- Srāvana Belgola.","Srāvana Belgola (India) -- Religious life and customs."],"publish_date":"1989","publish_country":"ne ","series":["Monographs and theoretical studies in sociology and anthropology in honour of Nels Anderson,","publication 28"],"by_statement":"S. Settar.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL3880160W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["60063953","17876059"],"latest_revision":10,"revision":10,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-11-06T12:35:20.981229"}}},"ISBN:9781784532642":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781784532642","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28591850M/Dharma","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28591850M/Dharma","details":{"publishers":["I. B. Tauris & Company, Limited"],"subtitle":"The Hindu, Buddhist, Jain and Sikh Traditions of India","last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-05T01:18:43.278086"},"source_records":["bwb:9781784532642"],"title":"Dharma","number_of_pages":304,"isbn_13":["9781784532642"],"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-05T01:18:43.278086"},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"full_title":"Dharma The Hindu, Buddhist, Jain and Sikh Traditions of India","lc_classifications":["B132.D5"],"publish_date":"2017","key":"/books/OL28591850M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7115214A","name":"Veena R. Howard"},{"key":"/authors/OL8085772A","name":"Rita D. Sherma"}],"latest_revision":1,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21122446W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Dharma"],"revision":1}},"ISBN:9781784532635":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781784532635","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28591846M/Dharma","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28591846M/Dharma","details":{"publishers":["I. B. Tauris & Company, Limited"],"subtitle":"The Hindu, Buddhist, Jain and Sikh Traditions of India","source_records":["bwb:9781784532635","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-026.mrc:112860957:1918","marc:marc_bloomsbury/2025MAR_bloomsbury.mrc:29915628:4227","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_025.bib.mrc:41741581:3247"],"title":"Dharma","number_of_pages":304,"isbn_13":["9781784532635"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"full_title":"Dharma The Hindu, Buddhist, Jain and Sikh Traditions of India","lc_classifications":["B132.D5","BL2003 .D43 2017","BL2003 .D43 2017eb"],"publish_date":"2017","key":"/books/OL28591846M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7115214A","name":"Veena R. Howard"},{"key":"/authors/OL8085772A","name":"Rita D. Sherma"}],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21122446W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Dharma"],"oclc_numbers":["894025779","1007701654"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Dharma is central to all the indigenous religious traditions of India, which cannot adequately be understood apart from it. Often translated as \"ethics\", \"religion\" or \"religious law\", dharma possesses elements of each of these but is not confined to any single category. Neither is it the equivalent of what many in the West might usually consider to be \"a philosophy\". This much-needed analysis of the history and heritage of dharma shows that it is instead a multi-faceted religious force, or paradigm, that has defined and that continues to shape the different cultures and civilizations of South Asia in a whole multitude of forms, organizing many aspects of life. Experts in the fields of Hindu, Jain, Buddhist, and Sikh studies here bring fresh insights to dharma in terms both of its distinctiveness and its commonality as these are expressed across, and between, the several religions of the subcontinent. Exploring ethics, practice, history, and social and gender issues, the contributors engage critically with some prevalent and often problematic interpretations of dharma, and point to new ways of appreciating these traditions in a manner that is appropriate to and thoroughly consistent with their varied internal debates, practices and self-representations.\"--"},"identifiers":{"doi":["10.5040/9781350986084"]},"latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-05T01:18:39.463162"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-12-16T12:12:45.020135"}}},"ISBN:9781350224742":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781350224742","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL35559497M/Dharma","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL35559497M/Dharma","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7115214A","name":"Veena R. Howard"}],"isbn_13":["9781350224742"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["B132.D5"],"pagination":"304","publish_date":"2021","publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"source_records":["bwb:9781350224742"],"subjects":["Philosophy"],"title":"Dharma","weight":"0.427","subtitle":"The Hindu, Jain, Buddhist and Sikh Traditions of India","full_title":"Dharma The Hindu, Jain, Buddhist and Sikh Traditions of India","works":[{"key":"/works/OL21122446W"}],"key":"/books/OL35559497M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-11-03T05:06:59.032448"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-11-03T05:06:59.032448"}}},"ISBN:9781786722126":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781786722126","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL51035486M/Dharma","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http